{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwGramDetSquareClass","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwGramDetSquareClass","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwGramDetNonzero","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RegTraceGramBasisChange"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.twGram_det_ne_zero_of_blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.twGram_det_ne_zero_of_blocks","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwGramDetSquareClass.lean#L91-L113","doc":"**Non-vanishing, by a route that goes THROUGH the determinant.**\n\n`QOU.Hecke.TwGramDetNonzero.twGram_det_ne_zero` reaches the same conclusion without ever\ncomputing a determinant, via semisimplicity and the converse of the Gram criterion.  This\nderives it from the square-class formula instead: the change-of-basis factor is a unit\n(`isUnit_det_basis_toMatrix`) and each block contributes `± d_λ^(d_λ²)`, so the product is\nnonzero as soon as no block dimension dies in `K`.\n\nThe hypothesis is exactly the one `regTraceGram_pi_matrix_det_ne_zero_iff` shows is *sharp*.\nIt is true in characteristic zero — every shape admits a standard tableau, so `0 < d_λ` — but\nthat is **not proved here**, which is why it is a hypothesis rather than an instance argument.\nTwo independent arguments landing on the same conclusion is a real cross-check; neither is\nderived from the other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.twGram_det_eq_sq_mul_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.twGram_det_eq_sq_mul_prod","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwGramDetSquareClass.lean#L62-L89","doc":"**The `T_w` Gram determinant is a square times the derived integer constant.**\n\nThe Wedderburn blocks of `H_{n+1}` are indexed by partitions `λ` of `n + 1`, with block\ndimension `d_λ` the number of standard Young tableaux of shape `λ`; the constant is\n`∏_λ ± d_λ^(d_λ²)`.\n\nThe square is the change of basis from `T_w` to the matrix-unit basis pulled back along\n`(skeinIwahoriEquiv).symm.trans heckeWedderburn` — the same composition\n`twGram_det_ne_zero` feeds to the non-vanishing criterion.  It is **not evaluated**; see the\nmodule docstring on why no statement of this shape can remove it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.blockIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.blockIdx","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwGramDetSquareClass.lean#L56-L60","doc":"**The Wedderburn block index at `λ`** — standard Young tableaux of shape `λ`, whose\ncardinality `d_λ` is the block dimension.  A `reducible` abbreviation, so it unifies with the\n`heckeWedderburn` codomain definitionally; it exists to keep the statement below readable. ","signatureChunk":0}]}